analyses.4:
All 9 trials scored 0 on dev, and also 0 on training success in the last 10% of training. Many things were changed across them: the recipe (1, 2 and 4 epochs; gamma 0.95 to 0.99; entropy 0.005 to 0.02), the head (pooled, exact footprint conv, per-layer gated) and the layout assumptions (dense remap, plain MLP, mask as input). None of these changed the result, so there is no gradient to follow. Dense heads that make no assumption about the action layout also failed, so a simple index or axis mismatch is not the likely cause. More likely the task is hard at this budget, or the world differs in a way that no input feature tried so far has exposed. For this final round I am taking three different shots that each maximise learning efficiency:
- a deeper equivariant conv network that also reads the legal-action mask as spatial maps;
- a cell-token transformer with global attention;
- the cheapest network (full sample budget) with a sharper policy: low entropy, short horizon, higher learning rate.
